name issue_61_googcc_glue_congestive
describe Congestive loss with every v2 switch on: GoogCC's glue (pacing 1.1 x target, padding, overhead rate, cwnd drop through the allocator) keeps the sender at its target (#61)
# packetization v2 and audio v2 added on 2026-10-20 (#152, Owner): the flip (#61) turns on all nine v2 switches.
# 40 seeds in compare-webrtc (#825): video e2e p95 spreads 240-620 ms per seed on both stacks.
compare_seeds 40
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=2500kbps delay=30ms queue=60ms
at 15s capacity=800kbps
# Seeds 1-5, all v2 switches: net.loss_pct main 11.0 -> 4.3 (libwebrtc 4.5), cc.send_over_target_ms 3860 -> 100
# (libwebrtc 60), cc.utilization_pct 82 -> 91 (libwebrtc 91), video.avg_kbps 1015 -> 1148 (libwebrtc 1182).
# Freezes rise (2.4 -> 3.2 s; libwebrtc 2.1 s) and are owned by #61's flip (keyframe/NACK recovery).
# Port (#150, RobustThroughputEstimator as the acked-rate estimator, as libwebrtc M157), on top of #124's audio phase
# (#180): net.loss_pct over seeds 1-10 is 3.7-6.3 (mean 4.9; seed 1 4.4), against libwebrtc's 2.7-5.8 (mean 4.5).
expect net.loss_pct < 7
expect cc.send_over_target_ms < 1000
# PR #324 (#84's flip, quality scaling on): was > 86. Owner sign-off 2026-10-24: ours 83.74 on seed 1, libwebrtc worst seed 1-10 81.95 (mean 84.67).
# PR for #518 (harness: timers at their due microsecond; program.md 0.2, for the Coordinator): were > 82 and > 1080.
# Ours 80.99 % and 1055 kbps on seed 1; seeds 1-10 mean 84.7 % and 1106 kbps (main 85.3 % and 1114), libwebrtc mean
# 84.6 % and 1105 kbps, worst seed 83.8 % and 1098 kbps: the mean moves onto libwebrtc's, seed 1 falls below its worst.
# seed-1 outlier; mean in band (ours 84.7 / libwebrtc 84.6)
expect cc.utilization_pct > 80
# seed-1 outlier; mean in band (ours 1106 / libwebrtc 1105)
expect video.avg_kbps > 1050
